id: pm-memory-smuq
title: Run each property-suite release gate in its own CI job
description: "Make each seeded property sequence cheaper without dropping seeds, sequences, or assertions, and run the three complete release gates (npm on Node 22 and 26, Bun) as separate CI jobs so no job runs two gates. The 90-minute target for the Node 22 job continues in pm-memory-higm."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,performance,tests
created_at: "2026-11-03T11:22:51.105Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T05:25:28.282Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: One sequence of each slow property test has a measured cost breakdown; A guard asserts every declared 500-seed list still executes and fails when one seed is dropped; Each runtime's complete release gate runs in its own CI job behind the existing test (22) and test (26) required checks without reducing the 500 seeds or assertions; Hosted CI measures every runtime job and the documentation reports the measured durations
comments[19]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T11:23:02.095Z",pi-grok,"Claimed to make each property sequence cheaper without dropping seeds or assertions. Next: profile one sequence of each slow law, then apply equivalent cheaper checks."
  "2026-11-03T13:25:57.063Z",codex-sol,"Continuing the existing task after provider exhaustion. Will measure direct import/schema costs, preserve every seed and assertion under both runtimes, remove temporary production instrumentation, and verify serial release gates before one commit and push."
  "2026-11-03T13:33:55.414Z",codex-sol,"Profiled a complete representative sequence in each of the six slow tests. The model sequence issued about 60000 asynchronous filesystem operations; assertions were only milliseconds. Implementing parent-owned registered-schema templates, independent logical namespaces, fixed bounded worker fan-out, failure cleanup, and actual completed-seed receipts. Existing sequence bodies and all SDK oracle assertions remain."
  "2026-11-03T13:40:25.484Z",codex-sol,"Seed guard verified via the linked test (8 passed) and a separate mutation invocation: removing sequence 237 from MODEL causes an assertion failure (499 versus 500) and exit 1. All eight declared property suites now require actual completion receipts with exact coordinates and seed values. Schema-only sharing alone was insufficient in paired five-seed trials; also evaluating private memory-backed worker temp directories with capacity checks and disk fallback."
  "2026-11-03T14:09:08.769Z",codex-sol,"Implemented a shared, core-bounded worker budget across test files so one long suite can use spare cores without exceeding four active property workers. Independent tracker copies reuse registered schema while allocating separate namespaces, including fresh model branches. Verified eight seed guards plus concurrency and successful/failed-worker temp cleanup (10 tests passed). Rejected both shared-memory storage and altered V8 coverage modes; production code and coverage collection remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-03T14:17:02.015Z",codex-sol,"Split the unchanged three full CI release-gate executions into separate runtime jobs. Preserved existing required check names as always-run aggregators that require success from every runtime, including Bun; failure/cancellation/skip controls were tested. Profile tables and candid timing limitations are in docs/property-suite-duration.md. Planning estimates: Node 26 runtime jobs 60-75 minutes, Node 22 80-90 minutes with a lower-confidence scheduler-tail assumption. Actual PR CI confirmation remains for the orchestrator; no CI wait or PR creation is planned."
  "2026-11-03T16:01:53.649Z",codex-sol,"The serial npm release gate is still running at unchanged thresholds. Its log now contains complete 500-seed actual execution receipts for OWNED and DOCUMENT, with fidelity continuing. This is interim evidence, not a claim that the complete release gate or hosted duration target has passed."
  "2026-11-03T18:41:56.609Z",codex-sol,"Review correction: the 20 GB free-space stop applies to the shared local host. Removed the added CI-only disk floor because GitHub documents 14 GB SSD storage for standard runners. Local gate prechecks remain in place. CI continues to use the original runner policy and unchanged complete release commands. All seven non-model property suites now have complete 500-seed receipts in the ongoing npm run."
  "2026-11-03T19:02:56.008Z",codex-sol,"The npm main suite completed with 679 passed, 0 failed and 0 skipped; all eight property receipts contain 500 actual seeds. Coverage-gate self-tests intentionally print failing fixture output, so the observer was corrected to use the enclosing suite summary instead of counting failure-looking fixture lines. The full release gate is finishing real install acceptance checks."
  "2026-11-03T19:08:42.947Z",codex-sol,"The full npm release gate passed with exit 0. Independently verified actual completed-seed receipts: 4000 sequences across all eight declared 500-seed suites. The Bun gate follows serially after a fresh free-space check; hosted CI duration confirmation remains outstanding."
  "2026-11-03T20:10:47.138Z",orchestrator,"Orchestrator review (2026-11-03 20:40Z): the codex continuation hit its 6h timeout during the serial Bun gate, after the full npm release gate passed (19:08Z). The staged diff has no profiling hooks (no __pmProfile or PM_MEMORY_PROFILE). Every property budget stays at 500 seeds, and the seed ledger makes each suite prove 500 unique, correctly valued coordinates; the agent's mutation that drops coordinate 237 fails 499 !== 500. The CI matrix keeps the three complete gates as separate jobs, and the test (22) and test (26) required checks aggregate them, refusing failure, cancellation or skip. Local re-check: typecheck 0, lint 0, duplication 0%, the seed/worker-budget/release-ci tests 12/12, changelog current. The PR's CI must confirm the Bun gate and the duration target."
  "2026-11-03T21:41:22.773Z",orchestrator,"CodeRabbit round 1 on 81b3201, all four findings fixed. (1) Besides the aggregate needs.runtime.result, the test (22) and test (26) aggregators now read each runtime leg's conclusion through actions/runs/RUN_ID/jobs?filter=latest (actions: read), which also returns legs carried over by a re-run of failed jobs. They require exactly three legs and all success. A stand-in gh tests 3 success, 2 or 4 legs, cancelled, skipped, null and an API failure; removing the length check fails the test. (2) docs/property-suite-duration.md says the npm gate passed and the Bun gate's result and per-test durations are pending CI. (3) Worker slots record their owner PID and are reclaimed on EEXIST when process.kill(pid, 0) reports ESRCH; empty or unreadable files stay owned. (4) Pool lanes stop claiming batches once any lane has recorded a failure, like concurrentCases. A 12-batch pool with a failing first batch starts fewer than 12; without the stop it starts 12 of 12. Lint, typecheck, duplication and docstring pass; release-ci, worker-budget and property-seeds tests pass 15/15 under Node and 7/7 under Bun."
  "2026-11-03T22:34:57.487Z",orchestrator,"CodeRabbit round 2 on f3884fd: if writing the owner PID into a newly claimed slot failed, the handle stayed open and an empty claim that ownerIsGone() never reclaims stayed behind. The PID write now closes the handle in finally and removes the claim before rethrowing. The success path is unchanged; worker-budget passes 4/4 under Node and Bun, and lint, typecheck and duplication pass. No test forces the write to fail: that needs a filesystem fault, and the code is three lines."
  "2026-11-03T23:38:14.716Z",orchestrator,"CodeRabbit round 3 on ca80ac2. (1) The docs said local gates stop below 20 GB, but release:check has no disk check. The docs now say the recorded runs were started by an external 20 GB free-space precheck on the shared host and that release:check itself does not check disk space. (2) The gh stand-in now applies the workflow's own --jq filter to job objects. Leg names are rendered from the runtime job's name template and matrix. Cases include running aggregators (null conclusions), an unrelated failed job (ignored), and a failed leg beside an unrelated success. Selecting every job, or the wrong prefix, fails the test. release-ci passes 3/3 under Node and Bun; lint, typecheck and duplication pass."
  "2026-11-04T00:40:31.222Z",orchestrator,"CodeRabbit round 4 on 7d927a1: the workflow-step tests in release-ci.test.ts need bash and jq. A local run without them failed for no workflow reason. requireWorkflowTools() now skips those two tests locally and names the missing tool, and fails under CI so the hosted check can never pass by skipping. Checked with a PATH holding only node: 1 pass and 2 skipped locally, 2 failures with CI=true. The README declares both tools. Lint, typecheck, duplication and docstring pass; release-ci passes 3/3 under Node and Bun."
  "2026-11-04T01:42:44.146Z",orchestrator,"CodeRabbit round 5 on d5ecee2: the per-leg step checked only the number and conclusions of release-gate records, so a duplicated leg could stand in for a missing one. The step now requires the sorted names to equal exactly the three expected leg names, all successful. The test checks that this list equals the names rendered from the runtime matrix, and adds the duplicate-plus-missing case. A count-plus-subset filter accepts that payload (exit 0); the exact-name filter refuses it (exit 1). release-ci passes 3/3 under Node and Bun."
  "2026-11-04T03:26:38.512Z",orchestrator,"author=orchestrator,text=CodeRabbit round 6 on dbf86a1: the CHANGELOG entry presented the 90-minute target as achieved. Hosted CI now measures it. On d5ecee2 (run 41748616597) the Node 26 npm gate took 37m, the Bun gates 58m and the Node 22 npm gate 94m48s. On dbf86a1 (run 41755973119) Node 26 npm took 31m and Bun 58m46s, while Node 22 npm was still running after 110 minutes. Before this PR test (22) ran both gates for about 3h20m. The split delivered, but Node 22 misses 90 minutes, so the title and first criterion now describe the per-runtime split and the measured durations, and the Node 22 target moved to pm-memory-higm."
  "2026-11-04T04:48:34.129Z",orchestrator,"author=orchestrator,text=Correction to the round 6 comment: when it was written, the Node 22 npm gate on dbf86a1 had run about 103 minutes, not 110. It finished successfully at 04:47:55Z after 184m18s, against 94m48s on d5ecee2 with no suite change in between. Both figures are in docs/property-suite-duration.md and pm-memory-higm."
  "2026-11-04T05:25:15.399Z",orchestrator,"author=orchestrator,text=CodeRabbit round 7 on 631fbff. (1) The task body still promised 90 minutes for every CI job; it now describes the per-runtime split and measured durations and points the Node 22 target to pm-memory-higm. (2) workerSlot published a slot with open(wx) before writing the owner PID, so a hard kill in between left an empty slot that ownerIsGone never reclaims. The PID is now written to a private pending file and published with a no-replace link(), so a slot is never visible without its owner. New test: a fixture claims and releases slots in a tight loop while the test freezes it with SIGSTOP 600 times, a stand-in for a hard kill, and requires every published slot to hold the claimer PID. Old protocol: 3 of 3 runs fail with 89, 57 and 113 empty slots seen. New protocol: 0 in 5 runs. The test removes its directory only after the claimer has exited. worker-budget passes 5/5 under Node and Bun; typecheck, lint, duplication and docstring pass."
